<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_MiasmaWeather.xml                UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M4 build pass

  miasma_kit_spec.md M4: "RUT_MiasmaWeather WeatherDef - native fields for
  accuracy/movement (INVENTED: accuracy 0.85, move 1.0 - the muck, not the
  air, is the movement story; movementDifficulty 4 already prices that in
  biome XML)." Those two figures are the kit spec's own INVENTED values,
  carried over verbatim, not re-invented here.

  Zero rainRate/snowRate/sandRate is ban #5's linter-checkable half ("no rain
  weather reachable") - this weather itself can never produce rain or snow
  regardless of anything else. Ban #5 is fully closed this pass by
  RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock.xml (GameConditionDefs/) forcing this weather
  permanently via GameCondition.ForcedWeather(), which overrides vanilla's
  WeatherDecider outright - see that file and RUT_Miasma.xml's own updated
  header note for why the biome's kept Rain/RainyThunderstorm
  baseWeatherCommonalities entries are now inert.

  canOccurAsRandomForcedEvent=false (this pass's own INVENTED-BUILD choice,
  not the kit spec's): keeps this biome-specific haze from being rolled by
  some OTHER biome's "force a random applicable weather" incident.

  Overlay: reuses vanilla's own WeatherOverlay_NoxiousHaze class
  (RimWorld/WeatherOverlay_NoxiousHaze.cs, confirmed real against the live
  1.6 decompile - a WeatherOverlayDualPanner using the game's shipped
  "Weather/NoxiousHazeOverlayWorld" material) rather than commissioning new
  haze art this pass. The kit spec names this as an acceptable route
  ("via a WeatherOverlayDualPanner subclass or the greentide's
  RM_WeatherOverlay_GroundFog with warm textures - share the class, ship
  new art"); RM_WeatherOverlay_GroundFog does not exist anywhere in src/ yet
  (checked), so the WeatherOverlayDualPanner-subclass half of that sentence
  is what ships here, with vanilla's own hazy-green art rather than new art
  - a real, documented, zero-new-art reuse, not silently substituted.

  Sky colours below are this pass's own INVENTED-BUILD tuning (not the kit
  spec's, which gives no colour values): a green-gold cast at every time of
  day, all four sets carrying nonzero saturation per WeatherDef.ConfigErrors.

  ambientSounds intentionally empty: the kit spec's "ambient sound set
  muted/thick" (soundsAmbient) lives on the BIOME def
  (RimWorld/BiomeDef.cs:59 soundsAmbient, distinct from this WeatherDef's own
  ambientSounds field, RimWorld/AmbientSoundManager.cs:58-61) - picking a
  real SoundDef for either is a sound-design content call the spec gives no
  name for, left undone and flagged, not guessed.
-->
<Defs>

  <WeatherDef>
    <defName>RUT_MiasmaWeather</defName>
    <label>miasma haze</label>
    <description>A green-gold haze hangs permanently over the delta, thick with the Working's breath. Sound is muted, light is soft, and every lungful carries a trace of the muck's fermentation. It never, ever rains here.</description>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <favorability>Neutral</favorability>
    <canOccurAsRandomForcedEvent>false</canOccurAsRandomForcedEvent>
    <accuracyMultiplier>0.85</accuracyMultiplier>
    <moveSpeedMultiplier>1.0</moveSpeedMultiplier>
    <rainRate>0</rainRate>
    <snowRate>0</snowRate>
    <sandRate>0</sandRate>
    <overlayClasses>
      <li>WeatherOverlay_NoxiousHaze</li>
    </overlayClasses>
    <skyColorsDay>
      <sky>(0.72,0.70,0.48)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.6,0.58,0.4)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.55,0.52,0.3)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsDay>
    <skyColorsDusk>
      <sky>(0.68,0.6,0.32)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.55,0.5,0.3)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.5,0.42,0.22)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsDusk>
    <skyColorsNightMid>
      <sky>(0.22,0.26,0.2)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.3,0.32,0.24)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.2,0.24,0.16)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.7</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightMid>
    <skyColorsNightEdge>
      <sky>(0.3,0.32,0.22)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.35,0.36,0.26)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.26,0.28,0.18)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.7</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightEdge>
  </WeatherDef>

</Defs>
